<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranjit Vilas Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1907">1907</a>–<a href="/years/1914">1914</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranjit Vilas Palace is the palace of the former rulers of Wankaner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built on a hilltop above the town between 1907 and 1914 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> Sahib Amarsinhji. Its architecture combines Indian, Mughal and European Gothic and classical elements, crowned by a clock tower. It remains in the possession of the former ruling family.</p></div>
